r"""
Figure S4, panel b: the same at level 5, 1, 10 and 60 s before the labelled frame.

Panel id figS4_b_description_lags. No title is printed on this panel.

Redrawn from the panel's data folder, data/figS4/figS4_b_description_lags/
(DATA below), with numpy and matplotlib alone: what the panel shows is read
from that folder, and how the page lays it out -- the axes' rectangles in
page inches, limits, ticks, labels, titles, legends, colour maps, drawing
styles, and the decoration the data leave out (cage wireframes, category
outlines, category boundaries) -- is written below as literals, measured
off the published page.

Usage:

    python figS4_b_description_lags.py [--data DIR] [--out-dir DIR]

writes figS4_b_description_lags.pdf and figS4_b_description_lags.png (400
dpi), the panel cut from its page, into supplemental_figures/figS4/ (OUT
below); figS4_page.py draws the whole page and code/render_all.py every
figure.
"""

